<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The wedding collar's small lift in mood (2026-09-23), as a situational thought rather
		than anything on the hediff: in this game build a hediff stage has no mood field at all
		(`moodOffset` belongs to hediff comps and to thoughts), and the first version of this
		item put `<moodOffset>` in a hediff stage, which RimWorld reported as
		"doesn't correspond to any field in type HediffStage".

		A thought is also the better fit: it is what the mood list on the Needs tab is for, so
		the player sees "my wedding collar" there beside everything else that moves her mood.

		The stage's <description> is required, not decoration: RimWorld logs "affects mood but
		doesn't have a description" for any mood-moving thought stage without one - which is the
		one place a hediff stage and a thought stage disagree, since a hediff stage must NOT have
		one.

		The worker (PMM_Reptiles.ThoughtWorker_WeddingCollar) is active while she wears a
		collar, so there is nothing to grant or clean up.
	-->
	<ThoughtDef>
		<defName>PMM_Thought_WeddingCollar</defName>
		<thoughtClass>Thought_Situational</thoughtClass>
		<workerClass>PMM_Reptiles.ThoughtWorker_WeddingCollar</workerClass>
		<validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
		<stages>
			<li>
				<label>my wedding collar</label>
				<description>She wears the collar her husband fastened on her, and it suits her better than she would ever admit.</description>
				<baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
			</li>
		</stages>
	</ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
